Nethack doesn't compile out of the box. Compared to most other
software I have installed by myself it is one of the more difficult
ones to compile with its arcane compilation procedure.

For example on SuSE Linux, I not only have to edit
include/unixconf.h which is part of the "normal" installation
procedure for Nethack on a Unix OS. But I also have to change
src/Makefile because it tries to link against termlib instead of
ncurses.

Anybody who doesn't have a minimal knowledge of C and Makefiles is
completely lost when trying to compile Nethack.

